  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Dilution",
      "excerpt": "DILUTION If\nyou invest in our common stock, you will experience immediate dilution to the extent of the difference between the price per share you\npay in this offering and the net tangible book value per share of our common stock after this offering. Our\nnet tangible book value as of June 30, 2026 was approximately $(1.12) million, or approximately $(0.06) per share. Net tangible book\nvalue is determined by subtracting our total liabilities from our total tangible assets, and net tangible book value per share is determined\nby dividing our net tangible book value by the number of outstanding shares of our common stock. After giving effect to the sale and\nissuance of 657,000 shares of common stock in this offering and 657,000 common warrants at a public offering price of $0.75 per share\nof common stock and accompanying common warrant, and deducting estimated offering expenses payable by us",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    }
  ],
